    <cbc:Description languageID="ENG">The contracting authority has comprehensive and varied buildings, including schools, nurseries, health buildings, sports buildings and other buildings, including town halls, museum store buildings and older listed buildings. The total area is approx. 100,000 m². The contracting authority has a need for delivery of the following: Condition reports for buildings stated in the overview "Building 1st quarter 2026", annex 1 – Building and price overview.  Energy marking of buildings stated in the overview "Building 1st quarter 2026", annex 1 - Building and Price Overview. (The price for energy labelling shall be calculated in a fixed price for level 1).  A strategic maintenance plan for buildings stated in the overview "Building 1st quarter 2026", annex 1 - Building and Price Overview.  The contracting authority has limited budgets and it is therefore necessary that parts of the assignment become options on the contract, so that the contracting authority can decide which options the funds will be triggered after the prices are known. The contracting authority would therefore like the following options on this contract: Addition for level 2 for "Building 1st quarter 2026" (shall be priced and will be a part of the price evaluation). Condition reports for buildings stated in the overview "Building 1st quarter 2027", annex 1 - Building and price overview. (both a fixed price on level 1 and an addition for level 2 shall be priced and will be a part of the price evaluation). Energy marking of buildings stated in the overview "Building 1st quarter 2027", annex 1 - Building and Price Overview. (The price for energy labelling shall be calculated as a fixed price for level 1). A strategic maintenance plan for buildings stated in the overview "Building 1st quarter 2027", annex 1 - Building and Price Overview. (Shall be priced and will be a part of the price evaluation).     There may be a need for a new assessment on parts of buildings where condition mapping has previously been carried out. If the contracting authority triggers this option, hourly rates stated in annex 1 - Building and Price Overview will apply. The option can be used in the period from the first quarter of 2026 to the first quarter of 2027. The contracting authority and the chosen tenderer will jointly agree on progress when triggering this option.</cbc:Description>
